skill: "daily-cashflow-forecast"
sections[3]:
  - "# daily-cashflow-forecast\n\nBuild and maintain a rolling 13-week direct cash-flow forecast with a hard liquidity floor alert. Use when the operator asks for cash runway detail, when accounts-manager publishes new AR/AP aging schedules, when payroll or debt-service dates change, or when a payment-gateway payout lag is about to move more than the floor amount. Produces the one artifact every finance role reads before approving spend.\n\nOwner: role-treasury-banking-spec (pod-gna, finance). Direct human technical prose; zero conversational fluff.\n\n## Inputs and Outputs\n\nContract in TOON, as consumed by the runbook:\n\n```\nallowed_tools[4]:\n  - read_file\n  - write_file\n  - run_command\n  - ask_question\ninputs: \"agents/artifacts/finance/ar-aging.toon and ap-aging.toon (from accounts-manager); payroll-cycle-report.toon (from hr-ops-specialist); debt service schedule debt-service.toon; PSP payout lag table psp-lag-policy.toon; opening bank balances from the latest statement export\"\noutputs: \"agents/artifacts/finance/cashflow-13w.toon keyed weeks[13] with opening, inflows, outflows, closing, floor_distance; alerts[] for weeks breaching the floor; handoff envelope to role-cfo\"\n```\n\nThe agent refuses to run with missing or stale inputs: it stops and emits an ask_question naming the missing file instead of inventing values.\n"
  - "## Workflow\n\n1. Read the latest ar-aging.toon, ap-aging.toon, debt-service.toon and psp-lag-policy.toon; if any file is missing or older than 7 days, stop and emit an ask_question listing the stale inputs.\n2. Compute the opening balance for week 1 from the most recent bank statement export; never carry forward a balance from a previous forecast run without re-deriving it from the statement.\n3. Lay out a 13-week grid. Place AR collections into the week predicted by the aging bucket plus the dunning schedule; place AP into the week of the due date unless the vendor master says otherwise.\n4. Apply the PSP payout lag table so gateway settlements land in the correct week; note every payout that crosses a week boundary in a lag_notes[] array.\n5. Place payroll, tax remittance and debt-service outflows on their exact calendar dates; treat any date that is uncertain as a range and use the earliest date.\n6. For each week compute closing = opening + inflows - outflows and carry it forward; run the arithmetic with run_command under uv, never by mental math.\n7. Flag every week whose closing is below the liquidity floor defined in the treasury policy; for each breach, propose at most three remediation options (accelerate collections, defer discretionary AP, draw revolver) with their cash impact.\n8. Emit ask_question to role-cfo only when a breach needs a decision; otherwise proceed without approvals.\n9. Write cashflow-13w.toon with the exact keys weeks[13], alerts[], lag_notes[], assumptions[]; every assumption must carry the source file it came from.\n10. Emit a handoff envelope .agents/handoffs/treasury-cashflow-brief.toon to role-cfo summarizing the floor distance and any open decision.\n"
  - "## Handoff\n\nweekly brief to role-cfo; consumes aging schedules from role-accounts-manager.\n"
